WEBVTT

00:00.714 --> 00:02.114
♪ Men, men, men, men ♪

00:02.116 --> 00:06.702
♪ Men, men, men,
men, men, men, men. ♪

00:06.704 --> 00:07.703
Hello.

00:07.705 --> 00:09.989
I'm Charlie's brother Alan.

00:09.991 --> 00:12.291
I want to thank you all
for coming.

00:12.293 --> 00:13.292
I know this is

00:13.294 --> 00:15.277
a very sad day
for all of us.

00:15.279 --> 00:16.778
Speak for yourself.

00:18.298 --> 00:19.715
Okay.

00:19.717 --> 00:25.254
Uh, I understand that some of
you have "mixed feelings."

00:25.256 --> 00:29.141
Um... but I think
we can all agree

00:29.143 --> 00:31.260
that Charlie lived life
to its fullest

00:31.262 --> 00:33.462
and-and gave it
everything he had.

00:33.464 --> 00:35.147
Gave me herpes.

00:36.799 --> 00:38.650
Chlamydia.

00:38.652 --> 00:40.486
Vaginal warts.

00:42.305 --> 00:45.441
Excuse me, this is my dead
son we're talking about.

00:45.443 --> 00:48.777
I loved him and I'm
devastated that he's gone,

00:48.779 --> 00:52.581
leaving me with nothing but
my memories and my regrets

00:52.583 --> 00:54.867
and the listing for his
beautiful beachfront

00:54.869 --> 00:56.818
Malibu getaway
with three bedrooms

00:56.820 --> 00:58.420
and three and
a half baths

00:58.422 --> 01:01.090
and a beautiful
panoramic ocean view.

01:02.259 --> 01:05.260
Help yourselves to brochures
out by the coffee urn.

01:06.796 --> 01:08.213
Thank you, Mom.

01:08.215 --> 01:09.631
Um, anyway...

01:09.633 --> 01:12.501
Open house is Sunday,
1:00 to 5:00.

01:14.020 --> 01:15.837
Okay.

01:15.839 --> 01:20.225
Um, I'd like to take a moment
to talk about my brother,

01:20.227 --> 01:22.861
um, and his incredible love
for life.

01:22.863 --> 01:25.397
He also loved being spanked.

01:25.399 --> 01:27.682
While wearing
my panties.

01:28.818 --> 01:31.320
He used my panties to make tea.

01:36.025 --> 01:40.862
M-My point is, um, that Charlie
lived life on his own terms

01:40.864 --> 01:44.249
and-and never apologized
for who he was.

01:44.251 --> 01:45.551
Yeah, blah,
blah, blah.

01:45.553 --> 01:47.319
Why can't we
see the body?

01:48.871 --> 01:51.590
Yeah, I didn't come all this way
to spit on a closed coffin.

01:51.592 --> 01:53.542
Okay, I understand how you feel,

01:53.544 --> 01:56.812
but unfortunately due to the
circumstances of his passing,

01:56.814 --> 02:00.732
the remains aren't exactly...
spit-able.

02:00.734 --> 02:03.235
I have a question.

02:03.237 --> 02:04.770
O-Okay.

02:04.772 --> 02:07.489
Uh, I wasn't planning on
doing a Q and A,

02:07.491 --> 02:08.824
uh, but go ahead.

02:08.826 --> 02:10.325
Thank you.

02:10.327 --> 02:13.195
Charlie owes me $38,000
for some,

02:13.197 --> 02:14.913
let's say, pharmaceuticals.

02:16.332 --> 02:18.500
Who do I talk to about that?

02:18.502 --> 02:21.003
Uh, well, I think
that's something

02:21.005 --> 02:22.671
you'll have to discuss
with the lawyers.

02:22.673 --> 02:23.705
Yeah.

02:23.707 --> 02:26.258
I'd rather not involve the law.

02:26.260 --> 02:30.462
And now, uh, I thought
we'd take this moment

02:30.464 --> 02:33.915
to hear from the person who was
with Charlie at the end.

02:44.027 --> 02:45.694
Thank you, Alan.

02:47.397 --> 02:50.199
Charlie Harper was
the love of my life

02:50.201 --> 02:52.401
and a wonderful, wonderful man.

02:52.403 --> 02:54.403
Selfish pig.

02:55.955 --> 02:59.541
Sure, our relationship had
its ups and downs

02:59.543 --> 03:01.660
and the occasional
restraining order.

03:01.662 --> 03:03.212
But at the end,

03:03.214 --> 03:08.317
we ran away together to Paris,
where he asked me to marry him.

03:08.319 --> 03:10.185
I said yes.

03:10.187 --> 03:14.056
And the next few days
were the happiest of my life.

03:14.058 --> 03:15.724
Nothing could spoil it.

03:15.726 --> 03:17.643
Not even when I came home
from shopping

03:17.645 --> 03:20.412
and found him taking a shower
with another woman.

03:21.465 --> 03:24.466
That's our Charlie.

03:26.135 --> 03:28.637
But I forgave him

03:28.639 --> 03:31.874
because I loved him
unconditionally.

03:31.876 --> 03:35.477
So you can imagine my horror
when, the very next day,

03:35.479 --> 03:36.862
he slipped on the Metro platform

03:36.864 --> 03:39.081
and fell in front of
an oncoming train.

03:40.650 --> 03:43.368
Never cross a
crazy woman.

03:43.370 --> 03:47.673
I just want you all to know
that Charlie didn't suffer.

03:47.675 --> 03:52.027
His body just exploded
like a balloon full of meat.

03:53.162 --> 03:55.781
Thank you.

04:00.103 --> 04:01.303
I'm hungry.

04:01.305 --> 04:03.672
Anyone else hungry?

04:03.674 --> 04:06.508
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

04:06.510 --> 04:07.876
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

04:07.877 --> 04:10.577
&lt;font color="#00ff00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x01 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00ffff">Nice to Meet You, Walden Schmidt&lt;/font>
&lt;font color=#FFFF00>Original Air Date on September 19, 2010&lt;/font>

04:10.671 --> 04:13.371
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

04:13.372 --> 04:14.888
♪ Men. ♪

04:16.292 --> 04:19.494
Charlie was the best boss
I ever had.

04:19.496 --> 04:23.231
I needed a day off,
"Sure, Berta, no problem."

04:23.233 --> 04:24.599
I needed a couple

04:24.601 --> 04:25.934
extra bucks,

04:25.936 --> 04:28.470
"Sure, Berta, no problem."

04:28.472 --> 04:31.390
All he ever asked in return
was clean sheets

04:31.392 --> 04:35.811
and hosing the vomit off the
occasional drug-addled hooker.

04:39.349 --> 04:40.999
What a beautiful story.

04:42.185 --> 04:44.903
Can I count on you to keep
the house clean till I sell it?

04:44.905 --> 04:47.055
Can I count on you
to keep paying me?

04:47.057 --> 04:49.624
Well, there's virtually no money
in Charlie's estate,

04:49.626 --> 04:52.077
but I'll be happy to pay you
once the house sells.

04:52.079 --> 04:54.129
Then that's when I'll clean it.

04:55.031 --> 04:56.782
I still don't see
why we have to sell.

04:56.784 --> 04:58.066
I mean, he left it to me.

04:58.068 --> 04:59.401
Obviously, he wanted me
to have it.

04:59.403 --> 05:00.686
Can you make
the mortgage payments?

05:00.711 --> 05:01.604
No.

05:01.605 --> 05:03.405
Can you pay the property tax?

05:03.407 --> 05:05.573
Not per se.

05:05.575 --> 05:07.626
But I was kind of hoping
you'd help out.

05:07.628 --> 05:10.345
I mean, after all, your grandson
lives here part-time.

05:14.267 --> 05:16.935
Good job raising him.

05:16.937 --> 05:20.939
Uh, darling, I can't afford
to maintain my house

05:20.941 --> 05:22.891
and your house
at the same time.

05:22.893 --> 05:24.476
But you're my mommy.

05:24.478 --> 05:28.063
Good job raising him.

05:29.082 --> 05:32.317
Once I sell this place,
you can come live with me.

05:32.319 --> 05:33.601
But why would I have to?

05:33.603 --> 05:35.654
I mean, won't I get
a lot of money from the sale?

05:35.656 --> 05:38.957
Oh, please. Charlie had
three mortgages on this place.

05:38.959 --> 05:41.576
Once we deduct closing costs
and escrow fees

05:41.578 --> 05:43.795
and my commission,
you'll be lucky to break even.

05:43.797 --> 05:45.747
Wait a minute, you're planning
to take a commission?

05:45.749 --> 05:46.915
She doesn't work for free.

05:46.917 --> 05:48.383
Why should I?

05:51.554 --> 05:55.757
Don't think those silent ones
are fooling anybody.

05:55.759 --> 05:57.008
♪ Men. ♪

06:00.096 --> 06:01.730
Hi. I'm here
for the open house.

06:01.732 --> 06:03.148
Of course. Come right in.

06:03.150 --> 06:04.433
Thank you.

06:04.435 --> 06:07.302
Three bedrooms,
three and a half baths,

06:07.304 --> 06:09.988
60 feet of prime
Malibu oceanfront.

06:09.990 --> 06:12.240
Wait a minute, I
know this place.

06:12.242 --> 06:13.692
This is Charlie Harper's place,
right?

06:13.694 --> 06:14.659
It was.

06:14.661 --> 06:15.777
Then I can't buy it.

06:15.779 --> 06:17.446
Uh...

06:17.448 --> 06:18.430
What? Why?

06:18.432 --> 06:19.614
Bad memories.

06:19.616 --> 06:20.916
Charlie and I had this

06:20.918 --> 06:23.651
drunken threesome with a crazy
chick right on this couch.

06:23.653 --> 06:25.170
Sounds like a good memory.

06:25.172 --> 06:27.289
Yeah, well,
unfortunately she passed out

06:27.291 --> 06:29.441
and Charlie and I
kept going without her.

06:30.760 --> 06:32.660
Bad memory.

06:33.446 --> 06:36.431
Oh, the feng shui is great.

06:36.433 --> 06:39.451
I mean, the place just
oozes positive energy.

06:42.671 --> 06:44.306
It's not practical.

06:44.308 --> 06:46.274
The commute downtown
would kill me.

06:46.276 --> 06:47.609
Don't worry, sweetie.

06:47.611 --> 06:48.894
Just let the universe provide.

06:48.896 --> 06:50.845
The universe doesn't provide,
I provide.

06:50.847 --> 06:53.131
I bust my ass 80 hours a week.

06:53.133 --> 06:54.533
Uh-oh.

06:54.535 --> 06:57.202
Sounds like somebody
needs to meditate.

06:57.204 --> 06:58.320
Uh-oh.

06:58.322 --> 07:00.622
Sounds like somebody needs
to file for divorce.

07:00.624 --> 07:01.790
Really?

07:01.792 --> 07:03.191
You want to play that card?

07:03.193 --> 07:05.693
'Cause I will take you and
your uptight bourgeois family

07:05.695 --> 07:07.913
for every penny you've got.

07:07.915 --> 07:09.130
Bye-bye!

07:11.634 --> 07:13.885
Bye-bye!

07:16.689 --> 07:18.390
What a fun couple.

07:19.976 --> 07:21.209
♪ Men. ♪

07:22.596 --> 07:25.046
Sorry, the open
house is over.

07:25.048 --> 07:27.816
I got a package
for Alan Harper.

07:27.818 --> 07:29.050
Oh, uh, that's me.

07:29.052 --> 07:29.901
Sign here.

07:29.903 --> 07:32.103
Ooh, how exciting.

07:33.906 --> 07:35.056
Wonder what it is.

07:35.058 --> 07:37.242
It's from a crematorium,

07:37.244 --> 07:39.611
so that kind of
narrows it down.

07:39.613 --> 07:42.864
That's, uh,
that's my brother.

07:42.866 --> 07:46.334
Berta,
Charlie's here!

07:46.336 --> 07:47.669
Thank you.

07:47.671 --> 07:49.037
Enjoy.

08:20.152 --> 08:22.203
Well...

08:22.205 --> 08:24.272
here we are, buddy.

08:26.075 --> 08:28.560
Just like old times, huh?

08:28.562 --> 08:31.796
I'm talking and you're
in a bottle ignoring me.

08:36.769 --> 08:41.456
I, uh, I wanted to tell you,
uh, that I loved you,

08:41.458 --> 08:44.959
and I will miss you,

08:44.961 --> 08:50.432
and I will always be grateful
for you taking Jake and me in,

08:50.434 --> 08:53.585
letting us live here
all these years.

08:55.438 --> 08:59.474
So, now the question is...

08:59.476 --> 09:01.993
what do we do with you?

09:01.995 --> 09:05.497
I know what you said
you wanted, but...

09:05.499 --> 09:07.616
I really don't think
Pamela Anderson will agree

09:07.618 --> 09:09.817
to swallow your ashes.

09:12.538 --> 09:15.790
Um, I-I could take you with me
to live at Mom's,

09:15.792 --> 09:18.560
but that's how
horror movies start.

09:22.131 --> 09:24.015
Hey.

09:24.017 --> 09:27.185
Maybe I could sprinkle you
on the beach.

09:27.187 --> 09:29.671
I mean, it's simple,
it's dignified,

09:29.673 --> 09:31.523
and pretty girls
covered with oil

09:31.525 --> 09:35.026
will be sitting on you all day.

09:35.028 --> 09:37.195
Kind of like your life.

09:39.014 --> 09:41.199
Except for the dignified part.

09:43.869 --> 09:46.521
All right.

09:48.041 --> 09:50.208
Well...

09:53.196 --> 09:56.381
I guess now is
as good a time as any.

10:09.512 --> 10:11.096
I ain't cleaning him up.

10:11.098 --> 10:13.348
♪ Men. ♪

10:15.598 --> 10:17.031
♪ Men. ♪

10:17.185 --> 10:19.402
Can I use your phone?

10:19.404 --> 10:20.653
Sure.

10:20.655 --> 10:21.904
I guess.

10:22.756 --> 10:24.507
Are you okay?

10:24.509 --> 10:25.892
Yeah, I'm fine.

10:25.894 --> 10:28.594
I was just trying
to drown myself.

10:28.596 --> 10:30.730
Wait, you-you tried
to commit suicide?

10:30.732 --> 10:34.600
Yeah. But I had no idea that
the water would be that cold.

10:36.019 --> 10:37.320
Suppose I could've
worn a wet suit,

10:37.322 --> 10:39.722
but who tries to commit suicide
in a wet suit, right?

10:40.974 --> 10:42.075
That phone right there?

10:42.077 --> 10:43.109
Oh, yeah, yeah.

10:43.111 --> 10:45.328
Thank you.

10:45.330 --> 10:47.080
Uh, you got a towel?

10:47.082 --> 10:48.481
Oh, sure.

10:48.483 --> 10:50.816
Thanks.

10:54.654 --> 10:56.839
Hi. It's me.

10:58.459 --> 11:01.177
I want you to know that I just
flung myself in the ocean

11:01.179 --> 11:03.379
'cause I can't live without you.

11:04.681 --> 11:07.884
No, I'm not calling you
from the ocean.

11:08.852 --> 11:11.003
Because it was cold.

11:11.005 --> 11:13.523
I don't...
I'm in some guy's house.

11:13.525 --> 11:14.840
Um, Alan Harper.

11:14.842 --> 11:17.193
I am in Alan
Harper's house.

11:18.028 --> 11:20.480
How about it?
Will you take me back?

11:20.482 --> 11:23.282
Are you sure?

11:23.284 --> 11:26.452
You heard what I said
about the ocean, right?

11:28.572 --> 11:30.706
Okay, fine.
I'll stop bothering you.

11:30.708 --> 11:34.160
But I want you to know that I
will love you forever and ever.

11:35.028 --> 11:36.295
Really?

11:36.297 --> 11:37.780
That bothers you?

11:39.533 --> 11:42.752
Okay. Bye.

11:44.704 --> 11:46.305
You got a wet suit?

11:46.307 --> 11:48.925
Oh, come on.
It... it can't be that bad.

11:48.927 --> 11:50.943
It could be.
You don't know.

11:51.812 --> 11:53.712
No, no, I do.

11:53.714 --> 11:55.398
Come on. Come on.
Sit down. Sit down.

11:55.400 --> 11:57.183
Listen.

11:57.185 --> 11:59.902
I have been
where you are--

11:59.904 --> 12:02.738
uh, rejected,
friendless, broke.

12:02.740 --> 12:03.940
I'm not broke.

12:03.942 --> 12:05.724
I'm worth, like,
a billion dollars.

12:06.560 --> 12:08.611
Beg pardon?

12:08.613 --> 12:12.231
1.3 is what her lawyer says,
but I would give up every penny

12:12.233 --> 12:14.116
if she would take me back.

12:15.035 --> 12:17.587
No, no, no.
You don't want to do that.

12:17.589 --> 12:21.757
Uh... I think you can find a lot
of girls for way less money.

12:21.759 --> 12:23.092
I don't want other girls.

12:23.094 --> 12:24.410
I want Bridget.

12:24.412 --> 12:26.078
Right. Right.

12:26.080 --> 12:27.847
Um, just to clarify, um,

12:27.849 --> 12:31.300
did you say "billion"
with a "buh?"

12:32.470 --> 12:33.970
Listen, trust me.

12:33.972 --> 12:35.972
Money does not
buy happiness.

12:35.974 --> 12:38.824
I wouldn't know.
I've never had either.

12:39.643 --> 12:41.561
Come on.
You're doing all right.

12:41.563 --> 12:43.563
You're living in
a beach house in Malibu.

12:43.565 --> 12:44.647
I have to sell it.

12:44.649 --> 12:46.349
And it's not even mine;
it's his.

12:48.585 --> 12:50.570
His?

12:50.572 --> 12:52.488
That's my dead brother.

12:52.490 --> 12:53.906
Oh.

12:53.908 --> 12:56.576
I'm sorry I made you spill him.

12:56.578 --> 12:58.127
That's okay. That's okay.

12:58.129 --> 12:59.945
I'll DustBust him later.

12:59.947 --> 13:01.330
You know what?

13:01.332 --> 13:02.632
I'll get out of your way.

13:02.634 --> 13:04.300
Thank you for letting me
use your phone.

13:04.302 --> 13:06.168
Wait, hang on.
You sure you're okay?

13:06.170 --> 13:08.888
Yeah. I'm just going to go back
to my hotel room

13:08.890 --> 13:11.841
and update my Facebook status
to "not dead yet."

13:11.843 --> 13:14.010
Wait, wait, wait. I...
I just went to one funeral.

13:14.012 --> 13:15.978
I-I don't want to be involved
in another one.

13:15.980 --> 13:20.099
Why don't you and I go out
and have a drink and talk?

13:20.101 --> 13:22.134
About what?

13:22.136 --> 13:23.636
Oh, I don't know.

13:23.638 --> 13:25.137
The weather, politics.

13:25.139 --> 13:27.073
Why somebody would want
to kill themselves

13:27.075 --> 13:29.609
when they have
a billion freaking dollars.

13:29.611 --> 13:31.527
Come on.

13:31.529 --> 13:34.313
We'll, uh, put your clothes
in the dryer.

13:35.165 --> 13:36.482
All right.

13:37.751 --> 13:39.752
Oh, by the way...

13:40.587 --> 13:43.039
I'm Walden.
Walden Schmidt.

13:43.041 --> 13:45.091
Well, it's nice to meet
you, Walden Schmidt.

13:45.093 --> 13:47.426
Oh. Oh, sure. I suppose
there's no reason

13:47.428 --> 13:49.962
you can't undress right
here in the living room.

13:49.964 --> 13:51.464
Oh, Skivvies coming off, too.

13:51.466 --> 13:54.016
Okay. Okay, well, uh,
no body issues.

13:54.018 --> 13:56.185
Lucky you. That's...

13:57.137 --> 13:58.504
You're a good guy,
Alan Harper.

13:58.506 --> 14:00.339
Oh, and he's a
hugger as well.

14:00.341 --> 14:01.941
Okeydokey.

14:01.943 --> 14:04.110
I'll be right back.

14:06.346 --> 14:08.681
$1.3 billion,

14:08.683 --> 14:11.901
and he's hung like an elephant.

14:11.903 --> 14:14.520
♪ Men. ♪

14:14.522 --> 14:16.539
Uh, I will have
an appletini.

14:16.541 --> 14:18.374
Uh, and, um...?

14:18.376 --> 14:21.077
Oh, uh, ginger
ale, please.

14:21.079 --> 14:22.662
Really?

14:22.664 --> 14:24.046
Fresh off
a suicide attempt,

14:24.048 --> 14:25.581
and you're ordering
a ginger ale?

14:25.583 --> 14:28.200
Yeah. I don't like
the taste of alcohol.

14:28.202 --> 14:29.835
Nobody likes
the taste of alcohol.

14:29.837 --> 14:31.837
We like the effects
of alcohol.

14:31.839 --> 14:34.707
How it makes you feel tall,
good-looking and smart.

14:35.509 --> 14:37.560
I am tall, good-looking
and smart.

14:41.214 --> 14:43.382
Give him an appletini.

14:44.434 --> 14:46.936
So, just out of curiosity,

14:46.938 --> 14:50.156
how does someone get
to be worth so much money?

14:50.158 --> 14:52.358
Oh, it's pretty
simple, really.

14:52.360 --> 14:54.393
You ever hear of
Blungogo.com?

14:54.395 --> 14:55.661
No.

14:55.663 --> 14:56.895
And you never will,

14:56.897 --> 14:58.614
because Microsoft
bought it from me

14:58.616 --> 15:01.951
for $1.3 billion, and
then they bundled it

15:01.953 --> 15:04.587
with their iPod
killer, the Zune.

15:06.456 --> 15:08.107
Really?

15:08.109 --> 15:10.176
I don't think it
came with my Zune.

15:10.178 --> 15:12.445
You bought a Zune?

15:13.313 --> 15:15.081
I had a coupon.

15:15.083 --> 15:16.248
Cheers?

15:16.250 --> 15:17.967
Oh. Cheers.

15:23.273 --> 15:26.892
So, don't take this
the wrong way,

15:26.894 --> 15:30.713
but I can't get the image
of your penis out of my mind.

15:33.133 --> 15:35.618
Thank you.
That's very sweet.

15:37.070 --> 15:39.288
♪ Men. ♪

15:40.490 --> 15:42.074
You don't understand.

15:42.076 --> 15:44.943
Bridget was my
high school sweetheart.

15:44.945 --> 15:47.580
She was the love
of my life.

15:47.582 --> 15:48.998
So why'd she leave you?

15:49.000 --> 15:50.549
She catch you
with another woman?

15:50.551 --> 15:52.451
